Lota's Vulkan submit patch: a guard added to submitGpuCommands in LÖVE's
src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp. submitGpuCommands ends the
frame's command buffer (line 478) and then submits it (line 514). If
anything between the two throws, such as vkQueueSubmit failing (lines
515-516) or the semaphore that vulkan_semaphores.patch makes in reach
(line 499), present throws with the command buffer ended and never
submitted. Nothing begins it again until the next present succeeds, so
the next command recorded into it is recorded into a command buffer that
is not recording, which Vulkan leaves undefined. The error handler is the
first to draw after a present that throws, and LÖVE's
(src/modules/love/callbacks.lua, line 259) and Lota's both make a Font
first, whose texture records a clear into that command buffer
(vulkan/Texture.cpp, line 467 on): on
a OnePlus Nord N30 5G (Android 14, Adreno 619) the driver dereferences a
null pointer in vkCmdClearColorImage, and the game crashes with SIGSEGV
instead of showing its error, in LÖVE's own Android app as in Lota
(doc/contributors/upstream/025.md).

When the commands are ended but not submitted, this patch records the
frame again from its start, as beginSwapChainFrame records it once it has
the image (lines 1487-1518): it begins the command buffer again, which
vkBeginCommandBuffer may do since the command pool resets its buffers
(line 3536) and this one never reached the GPU, records the image
layouts' transitions from VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED, and keeps the wait
for the swap chain image, whose semaphore no submit consumed. What the
frame drew is lost with it, and the error that unwound through the guard
is the one present throws. It changes nothing when the submit succeeds.

Nothing in Lota can do this: the command buffer and the frame's state are
private to LÖVE's Graphics, and no function of LÖVE's begins its command
buffer again without first ending it. CMake applies the patch wherever it
builds LÖVE's Vulkan renderer, on Linux, Windows, and Android, to a copy
of the file in the build tree (ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love
is never written to.

Drop this patch when LÖVE's present leaves a command buffer that can
record after it throws.

diff -ruN a/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp b/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
--- a/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/graphics/vulkan/Graphics.cpp
@@ -475,6 +475,50 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	// If the commands recorded since the frame began end but never reach
+	// the GPU, because ending them, or submitting them, throws, record the
+	// frame again from its start, as beginSwapChainFrame records it once
+	// it has the image, without what was drawn. Whatever draws next, as an
+	// error handler does, then records into a command buffer that is
+	// recording, not into one that has ended, which some drivers crash on
+	// (ext/lota/engine/vulkan_submit.patch).
+	struct RestartUnsubmittedFrame
+	{
+		Graphics &graphics;
+		bool imageRequested;
+		bool submitted;
+
+		~RestartUnsubmittedFrame()
+		{
+			if (submitted)
+				return;
+
+			try
+			{
+				graphics.imageRequested = imageRequested;
+				graphics.startRecordingGraphicsCommands();
+
+				VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer = graphics.commandBuffers.at(graphics.currentFrame);
+				if (!graphics.swapChainImages.empty())
+					Vulkan::cmdTransitionImageLayout(
+						commandBuffer, graphics.swapChainImages[graphics.imageIndex], graphics.swapChainPixelFormat, true,
+						VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED, VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL);
+				if (graphics.depthImage)
+					Vulkan::cmdTransitionImageLayout(
+						commandBuffer, graphics.depthImage, graphics.depthStencilPixelFormat, true,
+						VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED, VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL);
+				if (graphics.colorImage)
+					Vulkan::cmdTransitionImageLayout(
+						commandBuffer, graphics.colorImage, graphics.swapChainPixelFormat, true,
+						VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED, VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL);
+			}
+			catch (...)
+			{
+				// The error that unwinds through here is the one to report.
+			}
+		}
+	} restartUnsubmittedFrame = { *this, imageRequested, false };
+
 	endRecordingGraphicsCommands();
 
 	std::array<VkCommandBuffer, 1> submitCommandbuffers = { commandBuffers.at(currentFrame) };
@@ -514,6 +558,8 @@
 	VkResult result = vkQueueSubmit(graphicsQueue, 1, &submitInfo, fence);
 	if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
 		throw love::Exception("Failed to submit Vulkan draw command buffer: %s", Vulkan::getErrorString(result));
+
+	restartUnsubmittedFrame.submitted = true;
 	
 	StrongRef<image::ImageData> screenshotImageData;
 
